.TH TVDINNER 1 "July 2026" "tvdinner 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tvdinner \- play IPTV streams from an M3U playlist, an Xtream Codes login, a Stalker Portal login, or an HDHomeRun tuner, with XMLTV EPG overlay and guide
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tvdinner
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIURL\fR
.br
.B tvdinner bookmarks
[\fB\-\-bookmarks\-file\fR \fIPATH\fR]
.br
.B tvdinner backup
[\fIPATH\fR] [\fB\-\-epg\-shifts\fR \fIPATH\fR] [\fB\-\-favorites\fR \fIPATH\fR]
[\fB\-\-bookmarks\-file\fR \fIPATH\fR]
.br
.B tvdinner restore
\fIPATH\fR [\fB\-\-epg\-shifts\fR \fIPATH\fR] [\fB\-\-favorites\fR \fIPATH\fR]
[\fB\-\-bookmarks\-file\fR \fIPATH\fR] [\fB\-y\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tvdinner
plays IPTV streams from an M3U/M3U8 playlist, an Xtream Codes login, a
Stalker Portal login, an HDHomeRun tuner, or a direct video/audio stream
URL, using mpv. \fIURL\fR may be an http(s) URL, a local file path, an
Xtream Codes login in the form \fIxtream://username:password@host:port\fR
(\fIxtreams://\fR for an https panel), a Stalker Portal login in the form
\fIstalker://host:port/portal/path?mac=AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:FF\fR
(\fIstalkers://\fR for an https portal), or an HDHomeRun tuner in the
form \fIhdhomerun://host[:port]\fR.
.PP
If \fIURL\fR resolves to a channel list (an M3U playlist, an Xtream Codes
login, a Stalker Portal login, or an HDHomeRun tuner), playback starts on
the channel given by \fB\-\-channel\fR, or the first channel otherwise
(use the program guide's channel switching, see KEYS, to change channel
without restarting). Otherwise \fIURL\fR is played directly as a stream.
.PP
EPG (electronic programme guide) data is drawn automatically from the
playlist's own embedded XMLTV reference where available (for an Xtream
Codes login, this is the panel's own \fIxmltv.php\fR export; for an
HDHomeRun tuner reporting a paid HDHomeRun DVR guide subscription, this is
SiliconDust's XMLTV API; a Stalker Portal login has no EPG support), or
from an explicit \fB\-\-epg\fR URL. EPG times are timezone-aware and can be
corrected with \fB\-\-time-shift\fR for feeds that report incorrect times.
.PP
.B tvdinner bookmarks
opens an interactive terminal table of saved playlists instead of playing
one directly: \fBa\fR adds an entry (description, M3U URL, optional EPG
URL, optional default channel e.g. \fICNN\fR), \fBe\fR edits the selected
one, \fBd\fR deletes it (with confirmation), and \fBENTER\fR launches
.B tvdinner
with it, exactly as if its URL/\fB\-\-epg\fR/\fB\-\-channel\fR had been
typed directly.
Saved to \fI~/.config/tvdinner/bookmarks.json\fR by default.
.PP
.B tvdinner backup
writes the EPG shifts, favorites, and bookmarks files into a single
compressed archive for offline storage or moving to another machine
(default filename: \fItvdinner\-backup\-<timestamp>.zip\fR in the current
directory; the EPG cache and log file are deliberately left out, since
they're disposable, not configuration).
.B tvdinner restore
extracts a backup archive back onto disk, overwriting the current files
\-\- it prompts for confirmation unless \fB\-y\fR/\fB\-\-yes\fR is given.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Show a help message and exit.
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-channel\fR \fICHANNEL\fR
Channel name (or 1-based index) to play; defaults to the first channel
in the playlist.
.TP
\fB\-\-list\fR
List channels in the playlist and exit without playing.
.TP
\fB\-\-epg\fR \fIURL\fR
XMLTV EPG URL or local file, overriding any EPG source discovered in the
M3U playlist.
.TP
\fB\-\-tz\fR \fINAME\fR
IANA timezone for displaying EPG times, e.g. \fIEurope/London\fR (default:
system local timezone).
.TP
\fB\-\-time\-shift\fR \fISHIFT\fR
Correct EPG feed clock errors, e.g. \fI+1h\fR, \fI\-30m\fR, or minutes as a
plain integer. Applies to any channel without its own override in
\fB\-\-epg\-shifts\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-epg\-shifts\fR \fIPATH\fR
JSON file mapping a channel's display name (as shown by \fB\-\-list\fR) to
a per-channel EPG time-shift override, for feeds where different channels
are off by different amounts, e.g.:
.RS
.nf
{"BBC One": "+1h", "TCM US West": "-3h"}
.fi
.RE
Keyed by display name rather than tvg_id, since real-world playlists
commonly have several distinct channels (e.g. an East/West regional pair)
sharing one tvg_id for EPG mapping, which a tvg_id-keyed override couldn't
tell apart.
.PP
Default: \fI~/.config/tvdinner/epg_shifts.json\fR. A missing file is not
an error; malformed entries are reported as warnings and skipped rather
than preventing startup. Can also be adjusted live with the \fB[\fR /
\fB]\fR guide keybinding, see KEYS.
.TP
\fB\-\-favorites\fR \fIPATH\fR
JSON file storing favorited channels, keyed by playlist URL/path so
different feeds don't share one favorites list, e.g.:
.RS
.nf
{"https://example.com/playlist.m3u": ["BBC One", "Channel 4"]}
.fi
.RE
Default: \fI~/.config/tvdinner/favorites.json\fR. Updated live by the
\fBh\fR guide/playback keybinding, see KEYS.
.SH KEYS
While a stream is playing, in addition to mpv's own default key bindings:
.TP
.B i
Show the current/next programme info overlay, including video/audio
quality badges (resolution, codecs, fps, HDR, channel layout); while the
program guide is open, shows full details for the selected guide
programme instead.
.TP
.B g
Toggle the full program guide.
.TP
.B LEFT / RIGHT
Page the program guide's timeline back/forward by 30 minutes (guide only;
otherwise these seek the video as usual).
.TP
.B UP / DOWN
Move the program guide's channel selection cursor (guide only).
.TP
.B PGUP / PGDWN
Move the program guide's channel selection cursor a full page at a time
(guide only; otherwise these seek the video as usual).
.TP
.B ENTER
Switch to the selected guide channel and close the guide; while typing a
filter query (see \fBf\fR below), confirms it instead.
.TP
.B [ / ]
Nudge the selected guide channel's EPG shift back/forward by 1 minute,
saving the change to \fB\-\-epg\-shifts\fR immediately (guide only).
.TP
.B f
Open a text-entry dialog to filter the program guide's channel list by
name or group (case-insensitive substring match against either); ENTER
applies it, ESC cancels (guide only).
.TP
.B c
Clear any active guide filter and show every channel again (guide only).
.TP
.B h
Toggle the selected guide channel as a favorite (or the currently-playing
one if the guide isn't open), saving to \fB\-\-favorites\fR immediately;
favorited channels show a heart next to their name in the guide.
.TP
.B v
Toggle showing only favorited channels in the guide (guide only).
.TP
.B ESC
Close the programme details popup, or cancel an in-progress guide filter
query.
.TP
.B z
Cycle the video's display aspect ratio (Auto, 4:3, 16:9, 2.35:1, 1:1,
Stretch \-\- fills the window exactly, distorting the image if needed).
.TP
.B o
Toggle picture-in-picture: shrinks the window to a small, always-on-top,
borderless corner window, closing any open guide/browser overlay first;
press again to restore. Relies on the window manager honoring mpv's
placement request.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
List the channels in a playlist:
.B tvdinner https://example.com/playlist.m3u \-\-list
.TP
Play a channel directly by name:
.B tvdinner playlist.m3u \-\-channel "BBC One"
.TP
Play a direct stream URL:
.B tvdinner https://example.com/stream.m3u8
.TP
Log into an Xtream Codes panel directly:
.B tvdinner 'xtream://myuser:mypass@panel.example.com:8080'
.TP
Log into a Stalker Portal directly:
.B tvdinner 'stalker://panel.example.com:8080/c/?mac=AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:FF'
.TP
Tune an HDHomeRun network tuner directly:
.B tvdinner 'hdhomerun://192.168.1.50'
.TP
Manage and launch saved playlist bookmarks:
.B tvdinner bookmarks
.TP
Back up configuration to a timestamped archive:
.B tvdinner backup
.TP
Restore configuration from a backup:
.B tvdinner restore tvdinner\-backup\-20260101\-120000.zip
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mpv (1)
